#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
GNOME Adaptive Tone Daemon v3.3.0 (Native Extension & Zero-Overhead Pipeline)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Hardware-based Ambient Color Temperature (CCT) Matching for GNOME / Ubuntu.

Architectural Enhancements:
  1. Full GSettings Schema & GNOME Shell Extension Integration:
     Listens to org.gnome.shell.extensions.adaptivetone for real-time config updates (0ms delay).
  2. Master Toggle & Clean State Recovery:
     Gracefully restores GNOME Night Light settings when disabled via GUI/Extension toggle.
  3. Direct D-Bus GSettings Writes: Eliminates animation timer; lets GNOME's native
     Mutter/gsd-color hardware LUT smoothly interpolate color temperature.
  4. Suspend/Resume Safety: Subscribes to systemd-logind PrepareForSleep signal
     with a stabilization debounce to prevent D-Bus lockups / GDM auth failures.
  5. Zero-I/O Sysfs Caching: Caches hardware scale factors at startup to cut sysfs reads in half.
  6. Precise Direct Mapping: Maps ambient CCT directly to SmoothStep target with Hysteresis.
  7. Check-Before-Write GSettings: Only writes GSettings keys when values actually differ.
  8. Glitch Filter: Holds large ambient jumps (Δ >= 500K) for 0.8s confirmation window.
  9. Pure Event-Driven / Optional Polling: Toggleable fallback timer (Off by default).
 10. Real-Time Occlusion Guard: True time-based hold via time.monotonic().
 11. Crash-Safe Persistence: Saves and restores original GNOME configuration via state JSON.
"""

